  "request": "One immutable observation per group. Queued requests have admitted=0, effective_update=0, application_timestamp_us=0, update_result=255 and nis=-1; execution_result=11. Ordinary rejections retain their explicit execution result. No request counts as an attempted or effective fusion.",
  "completion": "Same operation_sequence as its owned queued request. Application equals resolved source time; evaluation is the actual publication present. admitted denotes an attempted valid numerical update. effective_update denotes accepted/soft fusion with effective gain or the existing explicit KF reanchor, never covariance-only inflation or NIS rejection.",
  "transaction_failure": "Emit fault status without successful completions. Output epochs retain the last committed output; failure_operation_valid explicitly distinguishes event failures including wrapped operation_sequence=0. input_present is the last accepted raw-input epoch; the record header retains the attempted cycle epoch. horizon_initialized=0 means primary/input epochs are unavailable (zero); output epochs still identify the last published state/P, including the preflight state before any horizon reset.",
  "numerical_revisions": {
    "kf6": 1,
    "eskf15": 2
  },
  "timing_mode": 2,
